hadiths[4]{hadithnumber,text}:
"18928","Waki narrated to us, Salamah ibn Nubayt narrated to us, from his father, and he had performed Hajj with the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, he said: I saw him delivering a sermon on the day of Arafah on his camel."
"18929","Yahya ibn Zakariyya ibn Abi Zaidah narrated to us, Abu Malik al-Ashjai narrated to me, Nubayt ibn Sharit narrated to me, he said: I was riding behind my father in the Farewell Hajj when the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, spoke. I stood on the rear of the mount, placed my hand on my father shoulder, and heard him saying: Which day is most sacred They said: This day. He said: Then which land is most sacred They said: This land. He said: Then which month is most sacred They said: This month. He said: Then your blood and your wealth are sacred to you like the sanctity of this day of yours, in this month of yours, in this land of yours. Have I conveyed They said: Yes. He said: O Allah, bear witness, O Allah, bear witness."
"18930","Abd al-Hamid ibn Abd al-Rahman Abu Yahya al-Himmani narrated to us, he said: Salamah ibn Nubayt narrated to us, he said: My father, my grandfather, and my uncle were with the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him. He said: My father informed me, he said: I saw the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, delivering a sermon on the evening of Arafah on a red camel."
"18931","Hasan ibn Musa narrated to us, Rafi ibn Salamah, meaning al-Ashjai, narrated to us, and Salim ibn Abi al-Jad, from his father, he said: Salamah ibn Nubayt al-Ashjai narrated to me that his father had reached the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and he was riding behind his father in the Farewell Hajj. He said: I said: O my father, show me the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him. He said: Stand and take hold of the middle of the saddle. He said: So I stood and took hold of the middle of the saddle, and he said: Look at the owner of the red camel who is gesturing with his hand, in his hand is the staff."
